## Delivery and privacy

Commit and push completed requested updates to the fork's current branch unless
the user directs otherwise. Keep unrelated work out of those commits. Audit the
entire outgoing commit range before pushing, including unpublished history.
Exclude credentials, personal filesystem paths, raw logs, local session reports
and log-derived channel/activity data. Publish generic documentation and synthetic
benchmarks instead. Use a GitHub noreply author address for new commits.

## Large-history cache and rendering performance

- `Channel`, `LimitedQueue` and `MessageViewQueue` support live per-channel history
  limits, borrowed GUI-ring reads, frozen pause snapshots, bounded similarity
  tails and a lazy message-ID index. Split header > Channel history is below More.
- `MessageContentPool` shares immutable Qt text/word-list payloads, including text
  in emote-bearing messages. Occurrence identity, emote elements and layouts stay
  independent. Its toggle and retained/cumulative accounting allow evaluation and
  rollback separately from the general cache changes.
- `debug/MessageCacheStats.hpp/.cpp` and `ChannelView` save rotating performance
  reports under `Misc/message-cache-performance.log`. Reports include stable
  session/view IDs, paint/layout timings, painted-row counts and content-pool
  savings. Unchanged views use a five-minute heartbeat to reduce duplicate output.
- `widgets/dialogs/CacheDiagnosticsDialog.hpp/.cpp` shows a scrollable, nonmodal
  report with Copy report. Keep diagnostics out of `QMessageBox::exec()`: the long
  report could block chat input while the native/auto-sized message box opened.
- `GifTimer` provides a shared 64-bit animation clock; `Image::Frames` computes
  the current frame only on demand. Do not restore per-image timer subscriptions,
  which made every offscreen loaded animation do work at 50 ticks per second.
- `MessageLayoutContainer` builds an animation-only element index after final
  layout ordering. Clear it when releasing or rebuilding geometry. Image loading
  forces a new layout generation, which refreshes the index.
- `ChannelView` preserves disjoint repaint regions for animated message rows and
  rebuilds released geometry when a hidden tab is shown again. Preserve both the
  partial-repaint and hide/show regression tests when merging upstream changes.
- Keep a bounded measurement-geometry working set in `ChannelView` for scrollbar,
  wheel and replay probes. Releasing it after every probe causes repeated shaping
  during smooth scrolling. Drop offscreen pixmaps; trim geometry after painting
  and release the set on hide or clear.
- Image-load invalidations batch over 20 ms. Periodic diagnostics batch over
  100 ms and write on a worker with bounded pending storage. Preserve per-report
  paint/layout spike counters and the shared event-loop-delay monitor; cumulative
  maxima alone hide later stalls below a startup peak.
- Details and probes are documented in `docs/message-cache-controls.md` and
  `docs/message-cache-performance.md`; tests cover images, layouts and channels.

This is a fork of an existing open source project with some custom functionality that was implemented for my use. Document the general status of each of them here to expedite future merge conflicts and to harden against future changes. When creating a new feature, make sure to add it to `.cursor\rules\my-update.mdc` and keep it up to date 

1. **Chat History / Reverse Search (Ctrl+R)**
   - **Feature**: Terminal-style reverse incremental search for previously sent messages. Press `Ctrl+R` in the chat input to open a popup showing message history. Type to filter results in real-time. Arrow keys or scroll to navigate, Enter to select.
   - **Files Added**:
     - `src/controllers/chathistory/ChatHistoryManager.hpp/.cpp` - Singleton managing per-channel message history with persistence to `Misc/chat-history.json`. Stores up to 5000 messages per channel, deduplicates consecutive identical messages, and provides filtered search.
     - `src/widgets/splits/MessageHistoryPopup.hpp/.cpp` - Popup UI for displaying and navigating history with search term highlighting.
     - `src/widgets/splits/MessageHistoryItem.hpp/.cpp` - Custom list item for rendering messages with highlighted search matches.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/Application.hpp/.cpp` - Added `ChatHistoryManager` singleton initialization and `getChatHistoryManager()` accessor.
     - `src/widgets/splits/SplitInput.hpp/.cpp` - Added `historySearchMode_`, `openMessageHistory()`, `updateHistoryPopup()`, `hideHistoryPopup()`, `exitHistorySearch()` methods. Modified `eventFilter()` to handle search mode keyboard events. Modified `postMessageSend()` to record messages to history.
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/HotkeyController.cpp` - Changed default `Ctrl+R` from "changeChannel" (now `Ctrl+Shift+R`) to "openMessageHistory".
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/ActionNames.hpp` - Added "openMessageHistory" action definition.
     - `src/CMakeLists.txt` - Added new source files.
     - `mocks/include/mocks/EmptyApplication.hpp` - Added mock for `getChatHistoryManager()`.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - History saves every 60 seconds and 5 seconds after the last message sent.
     - Popup shrinks to fit content (minimum 1 row, maximum 7 rows).
     - Current text in input is preserved when opening/closing search.
     - Non-contiguous duplicate messages are collapsed when filtering.

2. **Chat Control / Crowd Copy (Per-Split Ctrl+D Toggle)**
   - **Feature**: Per-split chat control mode that predicts a likely crowd message from recent chat and prefills the split input.
   - **Files Added**:
     - `src/controllers/crowdcopy/CrowdCopyEngine.hpp/.cpp` - Stateless evaluator for predicted message selection.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/widgets/splits/SplitInput.hpp/.cpp` - Added chat control state/timers, prediction updates, toggle handling, lock input behavior, mutual exclusion with reverse search, and visual active indicator.
     - `src/widgets/splits/Split.hpp/.cpp` - Added split-level crowd copy mode getters/setters and persistence plumbing.
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/ActionNames.hpp` - Added `toggleCrowdCopy` action.
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/HotkeyController.cpp` - Added default `Ctrl+D` keybind.
     - `src/singletons/Settings.hpp` - Added tunable crowd-copy settings.
     - `src/widgets/settingspages/GeneralPage.cpp` - Added Crowd Copy settings section in preferences.
     - `src/common/WindowDescriptors.hpp/.cpp` - Added split descriptor field for persisted crowd copy mode.
     - `src/singletons/WindowManager.cpp` - Save/load of split crowd copy mode.
     - `src/widgets/splits/SplitContainer.cpp` - Apply persisted crowd copy mode on restore.
     - `src/CMakeLists.txt` - Added crowd copy sources.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - Toggle is restricted to normal Twitch channel splits (`Twitch`/`TwitchWatching`) and ignored in non-channel/special splits.
     - Prediction uses time decay and per-user dedupe, is capitalization-agnostic for grouping, and preserves dominant capitalization variant for display.
     - Only ordinary user chat is scored. Channel-point redeems, highlighted redeems, announcements, watch streaks, notifications, and other non-chat events are ignored so redeem floods cannot dilute or starve a winner.
     - Initial winner can be immediate; later winner changes require confirmation window plus blank buffer before swap.
     - Prediction loop runs only for visible split tabs and analyzes a capped recent **user-message** count (`crowdCopyMaxMessagesToAnalyze`, default 100), over-fetching the snapshot so ignored events do not consume the cap.
     - While chat control is enabled, input is read-only and is cleared on disable.
     - `Ctrl+R` and chat control are mutually exclusive; reverse search activation is swallowed while chat control is on.
     - Reverse search now toggles closed on repeated `Ctrl+R`, with explicit handling to avoid shortcut routing issues.
     - One-time completion popup suppression is applied for initial autofill so Enter send is not interrupted.

3. **Channel Points Popup / Queueing**
   - **Feature**: Split-scoped popup for redeeming Twitch channel point rewards, with redeem queues. Opened from the split header (`PTS`) or hotkey. Talks to Twitch directly: GQL for loading rewards and redeeming, Hermes (the websocket that replaced PubSub on twitch.tv) for live balance and reward updates. Replaced the earlier bridge to an external miner websocket server (`localhost:8765`), which is gone and must not come back.
   - **Files Added**:
     - `src/controllers/channelpoints/ChannelPointsApi.hpp/.cpp` - Side-effect-free GQL/Hermes/device-flow request builders and response parsers, transaction ID generation and reward text normalization. Unit tested.
     - `src/controllers/channelpoints/ChannelPointsAuth.hpp/.cpp` - Separate sign-in through the Twitch TV app's device code flow (twitch.tv/activate), because Chatterino's own token can't use first-party APIs. Tokens are stored per Chatterino account in settings (`/channelPoints/accounts/uid<id>/...`) with a per-install device ID (`/channelPoints/deviceId`); rejected tokens are refreshed.
     - `src/controllers/channelpoints/HermesClient.hpp/.cpp` - Minimal Hermes client; connected only while there's a token and at least one topic.
     - `src/controllers/channelpoints/ChannelPointsController.hpp/.cpp` - Application-owned controller: per-channel tracking, redeems, queues, poll votes and predictions (used by the bars in section 11).
     - `src/controllers/channelpoints/ChannelPointsTypes.hpp/.cpp` - Reward/view-state types and `RewardBlock` evaluation, the single source of truth for redeemability used by both the queue and the UI.
     - `src/controllers/channelpoints/ChannelPointsLog.hpp/.cpp` - Logging to `chatterino.channelpoints` plus a persistent `<AppData>/Misc/channel-points.log` (rotated at 5 MB). Never log tokens.
     - `src/widgets/splits/ChannelPointsPopup.hpp/.cpp` - Compact popup: balance, sign-in state, reward search, favorites section, per-reward Redeem/Queue and status.
     - `src/widgets/splits/ChannelPointsConfirmDialog.hpp/.cpp` - Confirm dialog shown before every redeem, with Shift-to-keep-open behavior.
     - `src/widgets/splits/ChannelPointsFormat.hpp` - Shared cost/cooldown formatting.
     - `tests/src/ChannelPoints.cpp` - Parser, block evaluation and queue tests.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/Application.hpp/.cpp` - Added `ChannelPointsController` initialization and `getChannelPoints()` accessor.
     - `src/widgets/splits/Split.hpp/.cpp` - Added `openChannelPointsPopup()` and split hotkey action wiring.
     - `src/widgets/splits/SplitHeader.hpp/.cpp` - Added the `PTS` header button, shown for Twitch channels.
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/ActionNames.hpp` - Added `showChannelPoints` action definition.
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/HotkeyController.cpp` - Added default `Ctrl+Alt+P` binding.
     - `src/singletons/Settings.hpp` - Added `channelPointFavorites` (`/misc/channelPoints/favorites`).
     - `src/CMakeLists.txt`, `tests/CMakeLists.txt` - Added channel-points sources and tests.
     - `mocks/include/mocks/EmptyApplication.hpp` - Added mock accessor for `getChannelPoints()`.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - A channel is tracked while its popup is open or while it has queued redeems; closing the popup keeps queues running. Queues don't persist across restarts.
     - Every redeem is confirmed. The confirmed cost is stored and a reward is never redeemed for a different cost.
     - Transaction IDs are random (32 hex chars). A counter that reset on launch caused `DUPLICATE_TRANSACTION` failures after restarts. The same ID is only reused for up to 3 retries of an attempt that got no answer.
     - Queue modes: Once (redeem as soon as available) and Repeat (every time available, at least 3 s apart). After Twitch says "not now", a queue backs off 5/10/30/60 s.
     - Queued channels refresh reward data when it's older than 60 s (20 s while Hermes is down); data younger than 10 s is reused when a popup opens.
     - Reward text is sent as one trimmed line (line breaks flattened). Text past Twitch's 500-character soft limit is highlighted in the confirm dialog with a live counter, but not blocked.
     - The success sound plays only after a confirmed successful redeem. It's always the built-in ping since upstream removed the global custom highlight sound.

4. **Over-Length Twitch Message Display**
   - **Feature**: Incoming Twitch chat messages longer than Twitch's normal 500-character limit display the extra text instead of visually losing it. Characters after 500 are rendered as readable black text with a yellow background.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/messages/MessageBuilder.hpp/.cpp` - Detects over-limit incoming message content, builds the first 500 characters normally, and appends the suffix as highlighted overflow text.
     - `src/messages/MessageElement.hpp/.cpp` - Added optional per-text-element background color support.
     - `src/messages/layouts/MessageLayoutElement.hpp/.cpp` - Paints optional text-element backgrounds behind highlighted overflow text.
     - `src/providers/twitch/ChannelPointReward.hpp/.cpp` - Preserves redemption `user_input` from PubSub/EventSub payloads.
     - `src/providers/twitch/TwitchChannel.cpp` - Uses PubSub/EventSub `user_input` to hydrate queued channel-point reward messages when it extends the IRC text.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - Full message text remains in `messageText` and `searchText`.
     - Twitch emote parsing is preserved for the normal first 500 characters; the overflow suffix is rendered as plain highlighted text so the hidden payload remains readable.
     - Splits in the middle of a word avoid inserting an artificial space at the 500-character boundary.
     - Custom reward input normally enters as a `PRIVMSG` with `custom-reward-id`; PubSub/EventSub provides a richer redemption object with `user_input`, which can contain text not visible in the IRC payload.

5. **Chat Font Fallbacks for Special Characters**
   - **Feature**: Chat text uses explicit fallback families so special characters not covered by the selected chat font can still render.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/singletons/Fonts.cpp` - Appends globally installed fallback families to chat font family lists after Chatterino normalizes the selected font.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - Applies only to chat-style fonts (`ChatSmall` through `ChatVeryLarge`), covering message text, usernames, and split input without changing UI fonts.
     - `Gadugi` is included for Canadian Aboriginal Syllabics such as `ᗍᐈᐈᐈᐈ`, which FreeSerif does not cover.
     - `FreeSerif` remains included for other special characters.
     - If Qt does not already see a fallback family, the Windows font registry is used to load the installed font file with `QFontDatabase::addApplicationFont()`.

